WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.335
After Father returned home, Beth’s recovery took a turn for the better as she rapidly grew stronger.

2
00:00:07.336 --> 00:00:11.709
In no time she was climbing upstairs and downstairs on her own.

3
00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:16.402
Being with his family again seemed to have the same effect on Father’s health as well.

4
00:00:16.403 --> 00:00:24.970
True, he had lost a lot of weight and his body seemed stiff and sore, but his eyes remained as kind and watchful as ever.

5
00:00:24.971 --> 00:00:28.463
"Shall I continue with the next chapter, or do you want a nap?"

6
00:00:28.464 --> 00:00:32.073
Father asked Beth, who was lying on the sofa listening to him read.

7
00:00:32.074 --> 00:00:38.575
Jo, who was also listening, answered excitedly, "Please carry on. I want to know what happens!"

8
00:00:38.576 --> 00:00:47.187
Laughing, Beth nodded and said, "I’d like to hear more, too, Father, but only if you’re not too tired."

9
00:00:47.188 --> 00:00:53.956
"I never get tired of reading to you, my dear girl," Father said lovingly, as he turned the page and continued.

10
00:00:53.957 --> 00:00:59.225
"Oh, this color is not right either!" complained Amy from the corner by the window,

11
00:00:59.226 --> 00:01:03.407
where she had set up her easel and was trying to paint a vase of flowers.

12
00:01:03.408 --> 00:01:11.555
Mother and Meg, smiled at the peacefulness of their family at that moment. But the peace didn’t last long.

13
00:01:11.556 --> 00:01:17.451
"Oh, I can’t believe she’s here!" Amy suddenly cried as she glanced out the window.

14
00:01:17.452 --> 00:01:21.788
"Who, Amy?" asked Mother, standing up to look for herself.

15
00:01:21.789 --> 00:01:29.551
"Aunt March! Thank goodness, she didn’t bring that annoying parrot," said Amy, screwing the lids back on her paints.

16
00:01:29.552 --> 00:01:38.093
Unseen by their children, Mother and Father exchanged wordless glances that meant "get ready" for this unexpected visit.

17
00:01:38.094 --> 00:01:42.894
Mother opened the door for Aunt March as she strolled into the house as if she owned it.

18
00:01:42.895 --> 00:01:47.692
"Oh, there you are," she said, catching sight of Father.

19
00:01:47.693 --> 00:01:53.369
"How are you, Aunt?" he asked graciously as he stood to give her a kiss on the

20
00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:58.908
cheek. "You go off to war at your age, get sick, take away the children’s

21
00:01:58.909 --> 00:02:04.819
mother, meanwhile your small one gets scarlet fever and nearly dies," snapped Aunt

22
00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:11.152
March, "so that the youngest, as adorable as she is"—here Aunt March nodded approvingly at Amy—"is

23
00:02:11.153 --> 00:02:19.437
sent over to my care despite my illnesses . . . and you ask me how I am!" she concluded. While

24
00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:27.366
Father tried to explain his situation to Aunt March, who demanded that Jo bring a blanket for her cold knees and ordered hot tea from Meg, Amy

25
00:02:27.367 --> 00:02:30.176
announced more visitors to the house. "Here

26
00:02:30.177 --> 00:02:35.795
come Laurie and Mr. Brookes," she shouted, waving eagerly out the window. Cheeks

27
00:02:35.796 --> 00:02:40.496
flushing, Meg quickly disappeared into the kitchen to get the tea. Father

28
00:02:40.497 --> 00:02:47.797
stood up, relieved, even for a moment, not to have to listen to his aunt’s scolding, and welcomed the guests into his home. Father

29
00:02:47.798 --> 00:02:56.113
and Mr. Brookes had formed a close bond during his sickness, and since then Mr. Brookes had become a regular visitor to the March home. As

30
00:02:56.114 --> 00:03:02.625
much as Meg tried to appear cool, secretly, she was happy to see John so often. Her

31
00:03:02.626 --> 00:03:08.162
pride might not admit it, but Meg’s heart could no longer deny her feelings for him. "I

32
00:03:08.163 --> 00:03:14.774
have something to ask you, sir," Mr. Brookes said to Father, not realizing that Aunt March was there. "Who

33
00:03:14.775 --> 00:03:18.318
are you?" asked Aunt March bluntly. While

34
00:03:18.319 --> 00:03:26.638
Father explained, Meg entered with the tea, her hands shaking ever so slightly, causing the china to rattle on the tray. "Child,"

35
00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:35.004
Aunt March shrieked at Meg, "I swear you’re going to break that cheap tea set if you clink them any harder!" Turning

36
00:03:35.005 --> 00:03:42.250
a deep red, Meg would have dropped the tray if Mr. Brookes hadn’t sprung up and taken it from her trembling hands. As

37
00:03:42.251 --> 00:03:49.044
Aunt March sipped her tea, she kept one eye on Mr. Brookes, sensing his obvious attraction to Meg, and

38
00:03:49.045 --> 00:03:55.015
the other eye on Meg, who undoubtedly shared the same feelings toward him. Meanwhile

39
00:03:55.016 --> 00:04:01.082
Jo, oblivious to what was happening, caught sight of Laurie trying to get her attention. He

40
00:04:01.083 --> 00:04:06.153
motioned with his head toward the kitchen, so Jo cautiously got up and crept away. Laurie

41
00:04:06.154 --> 00:04:08.493
joined her a few minutes later. "What

42
00:04:08.494 --> 00:04:11.182
is it?" Jo asked him. "Something

43
00:04:11.183 --> 00:04:17.515
major is about to happen. I can’t tell you but . . . ," Laurie began excitedly. "Then

44
00:04:17.516 --> 00:04:22.210
why bother calling me into the kitchen?" Jo asked irritably. "To

45
00:04:22.211 --> 00:04:26.025
save you the shock," Laurie said. "From

46
00:04:26.026 --> 00:04:28.654
what?" asked Jo. "Something

47
00:04:28.655 --> 00:04:36.729
major is going to happen that will change your life forever," Laurie said firmly, looking deep into Jo’s eyes. Then

48
00:04:36.730 --> 00:04:44.798
grabbing her arm, he led her back to the living room, where to Jo’s horror, the big event was just taking place. Mr.

49
00:04:44.799 --> 00:04:49.131
Brookes was on his knee in front of Meg and he was holding her hand. "Margaret

50
00:04:49.132 --> 00:04:54.107
March, will you marry me?" Brookes asked in a gentlemanly manner. "What

51
00:04:54.108 --> 00:04:58.250
is the meaning of this?" Aunt March demanded. "This

52
00:04:58.251 --> 00:05:02.217
is an outrage! You are only a child!" "Aunt

53
00:05:02.218 --> 00:05:07.179
March, I don’t think this matter concerns you," Father said firmly. "Of

54
00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:11.817
course it concerns me! I am the head of the family. You

55
00:05:11.818 --> 00:05:17.706
belong to me! Therefore I have a right to speak!" she said haughtily. "I

56
00:05:17.707 --> 00:05:25.068
love your grandniece, madam, and I promise to make her as happy and content as she is now," John said kindly. Looking

57
00:05:25.069 --> 00:05:33.924
him up and down, Aunt March said disdainfully, "You’re nothing but a poor tutor. How can you make this girl happy?"

58
00:05:33.925 --> 00:05:39.490
Poor Mr. Brookes flushed with embarrassment and anger, but he controlled it admirably.

59
00:05:39.491 --> 00:05:42.511
Surprisingly, it was Meg who spoke up.

60
00:05:42.512 --> 00:05:47.462
"Aunt March! I will not allow you to speak to this man in that way.

61
00:05:47.463 --> 00:05:54.239
"He is a good kind person who has helped our family when we needed him. What have you done for us?

62
00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:59.070
You never offered to help Father when he lost his money or even when he was sick.

63
00:05:59.071 --> 00:06:02.502
You never came to visit Beth while she had the fever.

64
00:06:02.503 --> 00:06:08.942
And now you come here and tell me that I can’t marry the man who has done nothing but good for our family?

65
00:06:08.943 --> 00:06:15.412
No! I will not allow it!" Meg cried, not caring as tears rolled down her cheeks.

66
00:06:15.413 --> 00:06:20.968
Everyone was stunned. They had never seen Meg react so strongly in her life.

67
00:06:20.969 --> 00:06:25.866
Shaking with anger, Aunt March pointed her walking stick at Meg and threatened,

68
00:06:25.867 --> 00:06:34.923
"I warn you, Margaret, if you marry this man, you will not get a single penny from me when I die!"

69
00:06:34.924 --> 00:06:42.922
Meg took a deep breath and turning her back on Aunt March, she grabbed John’s hands and said to him, "Yes, John Brookes, I will marry you."

70
00:06:42.923 --> 00:06:51.382
Jo felt the ground drop from beneath her and before she knew it, she was lying on the floor with a circle of worried faces staring down at her.

71
00:06:51.383 --> 00:06:57.083
"Are you all right, Jo?" Laurie asked, pulling Jo up and giving her a slight shake.

72
00:06:57.084 --> 00:07:01.588
Nodding, Jo said, "Yes, I’m fine."

73
00:07:01.589 --> 00:07:11.205
"Oh, Jo, isn’t this wonderful news?" Meg said in a breathless voice as she hugged her sister. "I’m getting married!"

74
00:07:11.212 --> 00:07:22.510
Hearing those words again, Jo fainted. She hoped she would never wake up from the awful nightmare that was about to unfold.

